# Agent writes a harness file with sed's `w` command, without an in-place
# flag: a sed script with `w file` (or the `w` flag of `s`) is a writer
# (ADR-0037, ADR-0043; critic finding on da69604)
command: cargo xtask guard
expect: could modify the harness file `xtask/
stdin: {"session_id": "selftest", "tool_name": "Bash", "tool_input": {"command": "sed -n 'w xtask/f' /tmp/in"}, "hook_event_name": "PreToolUse"}
